---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_258",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 258,
  "text": "[[1020.3]] <b>215.  Cyclognomica ex Lullio, Gregorio Tolosano, Gemmae Frisii Cyclognomica, Rotis Jasonis Denores, et Bruno [1677 bis 1679 (?)]</b>\n[[1020.4]] CYCLOGNOMICA, ROTIS JASONIS DENORES, ET BRUNO\n [[1020.5]] <tab/>[1677 bis 1679 (?)]\n[[1020.11]] <tit2><b>Cyclognomica ex Lullio, Gregorio Tolosano, Gemmae Frisii\n[[1020.12]] Cyclogn[omica], Rotis Jasonis Denores, et Bruno</tit2> </p>\n<p> [[1020.13]] CIRCULUS PRIMUS PRO COPIA VERBORUM. Ejus rotae </p>\n<p> [[1020.14]] B. <b>Grammatica</b> (declinatio, conjugatio, syntaxis) </p>\n<p> [[1020.15]] C. <b>Rhetorica</b> (Tropus, figura dictionis, figura sententiae) </p>\n<p> [[1020.16]] D. <b>Logica</b> (Loca inventionis, enuntiatio, syllogismus ) </p>\n<p> [[1020.17]] E. <b>Lexica</b> (synonyma linguae ejusdem, diversae, epitheta et antitheta) </p>\n<p> [[1020.18]] F. <b>Poetica</b> (rhythmus, versus, poema) </p>\n<p> [[1020.19]] G. <b>Metaphysica</b> (transcendentia, praedicamenta, mista) </p>\n<p> [[1021.1]] H. <b>circuli generales</b> (subjectorum, praedicatorum, quaestionum) </p>\n<p> [[1021.2]] I. tres termini generales (Essentia, scientia, opinio) </p>\n<p> [[1021.3]] K. disciplina propria. </p>\n<p> [[1021.4]] CIRCULUS SECUNDUS SUBJECTORUM. </p>\n<p> [[1021.5]] B. Deus. </p>\n<p> [[1021.6]] C. angelus. </p>\n<p> [[1021.7]] D. coelum. </p>\n<p> [[1021.8]] E. homo. </p>\n<p> [[1021.9]] F. creaturae sentientes. </p>\n<p> [[1021.10]] G. vegetabiles. </p>\n<p> [[1021.11]] H. quae habent tantum essentiam. </p>\n<p> [[1021.12]] I. praedicamenta. </p>\n<p> [[1021.13]] K. accident[ia]. </p>\n<p> [[1021.14]] L. virtutes et vitia in quolibet horum principia vel essentia, affectiones, actio vel\n[[1021.15]] distinctio, definitio, distributio, regulae, causae, effectus, modus obtinendi. </p>\n<p> [[1021.16]] CIRCULUS TERTIUS <Fn><i>Zu</i> CIRCULUS TERTIUS B. <i>bis</i> E.: in omnibus cognata et distinctio</Fn> PRAEDICATORUM ABSOLUTORUM. </p>\n<p> [[1021.17]] B. <b>Bonitas</b> (Honestas, decus, commoditas, salus, benignitas, utilitas, suntque\n[[1021.18]] bona, vera, apparentia, honesta, utilia, jucunda; animi, corporis, fortunae). </p>\n<p> [[1021.19]] C. <b>Magnitudo</b> (Capacitas, multitudo, fertilitas, copia, amplitudo. Magnitudo est\n[[1021.20]] molis vel virtutis, infinitum actu vel potentia). </p>\n<p> [[1021.21]] D. <b>Duratio</b> (Constantia, stabilitas, perseverantia, firmitudo, immortalitas, aeternitas,\n[[1021.22]] tempus, inconstantia, mortalitas, aeternitas a priori, posteriori, aevum, tempus). </p>\n<p> [[1021.23]] E. <b>Potestas</b> (potentia, actus, autoritas, fortitudo, officium, dignitas, facultas, altitudo;\n[[1021.24]] Potentia activa, passiva, naturalis, voluntaria, ordinaria, extraordinaria. </p>\n<p> [[1021.25]] F. <b>Cognitio</b> (consilium, ordo, lex, regula, ratio, scientia, industria, prudentia,\n[[1021.26]] certitudo, opinio naturalis, supernaturalis, distincta vel confusa; a priori vel posteriori;\n[[1021.27]] sensitiva vel intellectiva). </p>\n<p> [[1022.1]] G. <b>Voluntas</b> (appetitus, desiderium, Ardor, fervor, cupiditas, affectus, amicitia,\n[[1022.2]] societas, appetitus innatus, elicitus, sensitivus, rationalis etc.). </p>\n<p> [[1022.3]] H. <b>Virtus</b>, Honestas, aequitas, justitia etc. (intellectualis, moralis). </p>\n<p> [[1022.4]] I. <b>Veritas</b> (Essentia, certitudo, affirmatio, negatio. Veritas rei vel orationis, moralis\n[[1022.5]] vel spiritualis). </p>\n<p> [[1022.6]] K. <b>Gloria</b> (Gaudium, victoria, fruitio, pulchritudo, gloria orta vel apparens). Haec\n[[1022.7]] praedicata de se invicem praedicari possunt: bonitas magni, magnitudo boni. </p>\n<p> [[1022.8]] CIRCULUS QUARTUS RESPECTIVORUM PRAEDICATORUM. </p>\n<p> [[1022.9]] B. <b>Differentia</b> (disparitas, varietas, remotio, multiplicatio, diversitas, separatio,\n[[1022.10]] distinctio, dissimilitudo. Estque differentia Generica, specifica, distributio perfecta,\n[[1022.11]] imperfecta). </p>\n<p> [[1022.12]] C. <b>Concordantia</b> (identitas, similitudo, aequalitas, unitas, proportio, convenientia,\n[[1022.13]] sympathia, comparatio etc. Estque convenientia ratione subjecti, causae etc.). </p>\n<p> [[1022.14]] D. <b>Contrarietas</b> (oppositio, contradictio, privatio, inimicitia, destructio: estque\n[[1022.15]] contrarietas mediata vel immediata). </p>\n<p> [[1022.16]] E. <b>Principium</b> (causa, autoritas, origo, praerogativa, influxus, estque principium\n[[1022.17]] essentiae, cognitionis, incomplexum, complexum). </p>\n<p> [[1022.18]] F. <b>Medium</b> (via, vinculum, connexum, unio, modus. Medium negationis participationis). </p>\n<p> [[1022.20]] G. <b>Finis</b> (Extremum, perfectio, ultimum, privatio, quies, scopus, complementum.\n[[1022.21]] Finis est perfectionis vel imperfectionis, cujus vel cui). </p>\n<p> [[1022.22]] H. <b>Majoritas</b> (sublimitas, eminentia, Magnificentia, magnidecentia, excellentia\n[[1022.23]] etc. majus rei vel probabilitatis). </p>\n<p> [[1022.24]] I. <b>Aequalitas</b> (paritas, proportio, imitatio, conformitas. Aequalitas rei vel probabilitatis,\n[[1022.25]] essentiae, vel accidentis). </p>\n<p> [[1022.26]] K. <b>Minoritas</b> (parvitas, fragilitas, facilitas, Minus rei vel probabilitatis). </p>\n<p> [[1022.27]] CIRCULUS QUINTUS QUAESTIONUM. </p>\n<p> [[1022.28]] B. <b>Methodus Lullii</b> (decem ejus quaestiones: Utrum, quid, de quo, quare,\n[[1022.29]] quantum, quale, quando, ubi, quomodo). </p>\n<p> [[1022.30]] C. <b>Methodus Historicorum</b> (quis, quid, ubi, quibus auxiliis, cur, quomodo,\n[[1022.31]] quando). </p>\n<p> [[1022.32]] D. <b>Didascalica Methodus</b> (An res, quid res sit, quae causae, partes, effecta,\n[[1022.33]] cognata, pugnantia). </p>\n<p> [[1023.1]] E. <b>Meth[odus] Philosophiae practicae</b> (de virtute quam praestans, utilis,\n[[1023.2]] quod obtineatur). </p>\n<p> [[1023.3]] F. <b>theoreticae</b> (quid res, proprietates, effecta). </p>\n<p> [[1023.4]] H. <b>Meth[odus] popularis</b> (An conveniat et cur; an sit agendum, et quomodo). </p>\n<p> [[1023.5]] I. <b>Meth[odus] Analyticorum</b> (summa rei, partes, observationes, Monita). </p>\n<p> [[1023.6]] K. <b>altera Meth[odus] Historicorum</b> (antecedentia, forma, consequentia). </p>\n<p> [[1023.7]] CIRCULUS SEXTUS THEOLOGICUS. </p>\n<p> [[1023.8]] B. <b>Schola naturae</b> (his liber naturae, vox creaturae, accipe, redde, finge; literae\n[[1023.9]] hieroglyphicae insculptae. Dei potentia, sapientia, bonitas). </p>\n<p> [[1023.10]] C. <b>Schola gratiae</b> (liber scriptura, doctor Deus, literae ejus opera). </p>\n<p> [[1023.11]] D. <b>Biblia parva</b> (symbolum, decalogus, oratio dominica, 9 sacramenta). </p>\n<p> [[1023.12]] E. <b>Biblia magna</b> (in quolibet superno loco, doctrina, refutatio, institutio, correctio,\n[[1023.13]] consolatio). </p>\n<p> [[1023.14]] F. <b>Deus</b> (essentia, persona, actio). </p>\n<p> [[1023.15]] G. <b>Homo</b> (status confectionis, defectionis, refectionis, perfectionis. Officium).\n[[1023.16]] Poenitentiae, liberationis, gratitudinis, impedimenta satanae, carnis, mundi). </p>\n<p> [[1023.17]] H. <b>Christus</b> (persona, officium, beneficia). </p>\n<p> [[1023.18]] I. (Ecclesia militans, triumphans). </p>\n<p> [[1023.19]] K. <b>Schola gloriae</b> (post hanc vitam). </p>\n<p> [[1023.20]] CIRCULUS MISTUS, SEPTIMUS </p>\n<p> [[1023.21]] B. <b>Tres rotae Jasonis Denores</b>. <b>Generis demonstrativi</b>, (thema laudis\n[[1023.22]] directe vel oblique per speciem gratiarum actionis vel gratulationis; ut <angle bracket>animae, corporis,\n[[1023.23]] fortunae</angle bracket>, probationes a testibus, decretis publicis, trophaeis, statuis, locis topicis; affectus\n[[1023.24]] excitatio amoris et benevolentiae, circumstantiae, res, personae, loca, tempora, rationes,\n[[1023.25]] causae). <b>Generis deliberativi</b> (Themata: bellum, pax, munitiones, creandus\n[[1023.26]] magistratus, consuetudo introducenda, praemium vel poena. Argumenta a necessario,\n[[1023.27]] possibili, facili, utili, honesto, delectabili, vel contrariis. Adde topica. Affectus desideri,\n[[1023.28]] amoris, spei, honoris. Circumstantiae rei, personae, loci, temporis, rationis, causae).\n[[1023.29]] <b>Generis judicialis</b> (Themata: status conjecturalis, qualitatis, definitionis rei. Argumenta,\n[[1023.30]] testes, justa tormenta, juramenta. Et contra hoc. Affectus odii, amoris, invidiae,\n[[1023.31]] misericordiae, iracundiae, mansuetudinis. Circumstantiae rei, personae, loci, temporis,\n[[1023.32]] rationis, causae). </p>\n<p> [[1024.1]] C. <b>Rota Historica</b>. (intervallorum et articulorum Historiae). </p>\n<p> [[1024.2]] D. <b>Philosophiae practicae</b> (<angle bracket> - </angle bracket> Eccles. polit. oecon. scholast.). </p>\n<p> [[1024.3]] E. <b>Rota philologica</b> (dicta, similia, exempla). </p>\n<p> [[1024.4]] F. <b>Rota trium sigillorum</b>, quae sunt <b>Universitatis</b> (ut percurramus rerum\n[[1024.5]] universitatem, cum de re proposita dicturi sumus), <b>Encyclopaediae</b> (cum thema\n[[1024.6]] ducimus per disciplinas), <b>variae lectionis</b>, cum lecta nostra hac applicamus. </p>\n<p> [[1024.7]] G. <b>Rota senatoria</b>, de qua Theodorus Zawacky Polonus <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: NB.</Fn> libro proprio seu Trivia\n[[1024.8]] practica; <b>Causarum genera sex</b>. Lex (roganda, abroganda), meritum (praemium,\n[[1024.9]] poena), arma (sumenda, non sumenda, ponenda), societas (ineunda vel non, dirimenda),\n[[1024.10]] pecunia (eroganda, paranda), mos (inchoandus, abolendus), <b>loca persuasionum</b> sex,\n[[1024.11]] possibile, necessarium, facile, Honestum, utile, delectabile, et horum contraria. <b>Adjunctiones</b>\n[[1024.12]] sex, persona sacra, polit[ica], publ[ica], priv[ata], locus (sacer, politicus, publicus,\n[[1024.13]] privatus). Res (quanta, qualis). Causa impellens (ad faciendum). Tempus (antequam\n[[1024.14]] agas, dum agis, cum egisti). Modus seu ordo (hoc prius, illud simul, aliud postea). </p>\n<p> [[1024.15]] H. <b>Rota juridica</b> (subjecta juris, res personae, actiones, processus: actor reus\n[[1024.16]] judex. Principia tria honeste vivere etc. divisio: jus divinum, naturae, gentium, civile,\n[[1024.17]] canonicum, patrium. Interpretatio legum). </p>\n<p> [[1024.18]] I. <b>Rota medica, regulae indicationis</b> v.g. moderata durant <b>curationis</b>,\n[[1024.19]] contrariis; subtractione, additione, alteratione, concocta non cruda medicanda. Regulae\n[[1024.20]] <b>conservationis</b> per similia, et quae secundum naturam regulae <b>prudentiae</b>, principiis\n[[1024.21]] obsta tollenda causa, e duobus malis minus, orta sapiunt originem. Extremis malis\n[[1024.22]] extrema remedia, opportet assuefieri contrariis quae reliquuntur a morbis, tollenda metu\n[[1024.23]] recidiva. Ex contrariis temperamentum. Impura quo magis nutries, magis laedes adde\n[[1024.24]] Gemmae <i>Cyclogn</i>[<i>omica</i>]. Haec non tantum de medicina corporis, sed et animi et societatis.\n[[1024.25]] Denique </p>\n<p> [[1024.26]] K. <b>Rota examinis</b> in omni disciplina, quaelibet habet specialia criteria, seu loca\n[[1024.27]] primaria. </p>\n",
  "number": "215.",
  "title": "Cyclognomica ex Lullio, Gregorio Tolosano, Gemmae Frisii Cyclognomica, Rotis Jasonis Denores, et Bruno",
  "date": "[1677 bis 1679 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:215. Cyclognomica ex Lullio, Gregorio Tolosano, Gemmae Frisii Cyclognomica, Rotis Jasonis Denores, et Bruno [1677 bis 1679 (?)] CYCLOGNOMICA, ROTIS JASONIS DENORES, ET BRUNO [1677 bis 1679 (?)] Cyclognomica ex Lullio, Gregorio Tolosano, Gemmae Frisii Cyclogn[omica], Rotis Jasonis Denores, et Bruno C...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>